-          "quote": "Under the hypotheses of [[def-regular-holonomic-phase-space-and-dynamics]], choose a local configuration chart $\\phi:O\\subseteq\\mathbb R^{d-m}\\to Q$ and write $T=D\\phi$, $G=T^TMT$. Then $Q$ is a smooth manifold of dimension $d-m$, and the cotangent coordinates $\\pi=T^Tp$ identify $\\mathcal M$ locally with $T^*Q$: the unique consistent ambient momentum representing $\\pi$ is $p=MTG^{-1}\\pi$. In these coordinates the restricted canonical one-form $p^Tdq$ is $\\pi^Tdx$, so the restricted two-form is $\\omega_{\\mathcal M}=\\sum_{j=1}^{d-m}dx_j\\wedge d\\pi_j$. It is closed and nondegenerate, hence is a symplectic form on $\\mathcal M$.",
+          "quote": "Under the hypotheses of [[def-regular-holonomic-phase-space-and-dynamics]], let $Q_{\\mathrm{reg}}=\\{q\\in Q:\\operatorname{rank}J(q)=m\\}$. It is a smooth manifold of dimension $d-m$. Choose a local configuration chart $\\phi:O\\subseteq\\mathbb R^{d-m}\\to Q_{\\mathrm{reg}}$ and write $T=D\\phi$, $G=T^TMT$. The cotangent coordinates $\\pi=T^Tp$ identify the part of $\\mathcal M$ over this chart locally with $T^*Q_{\\mathrm{reg}}$: the unique consistent ambient momentum representing $\\pi$ is $p=MTG^{-1}\\pi$. In these coordinates the restricted canonical one-form $p^Tdq$ is $\\pi^Tdx$, so the restricted two-form is $\\omega_{\\mathcal M}=\\sum_{j=1}^{d-m}dx_j\\wedge d\\pi_j$. It is closed and nondegenerate, hence is symplectic on the regular phase manifold.",
