-          "quote": "For consistent inputs in a compact regular chart, there is a uniform $h_0>0$ such that for $|h|<h_0$ the two scaled RATTLE equations in [[def-regular-classical-rattle-step-map]] have unique roots in neighborhoods of $$\\lambda_0=\\mu_0=\\frac12A(q)^{-1}\\bigl(D^2c(q)[v,v]-J(q)M^{-1}\\nabla V(q)\\bigr),\\qquad v=M^{-1}p.$$ The position root depends smoothly on $(h,q,p)$, and the momentum root depends smoothly on $(h,q,p,\\lambda)$ when the position multiplier is treated as a parameter. At $h=0$ the derivatives of the two scaled residuals with respect to their own multiplier variables equal $-A(q)$; they remain uniformly invertible for small $|h|$ on a compact regular chart. The branch derivatives are uniformly bounded there, and the roots define the selected local branches.",
+          "quote": "Let $C$ be a compact subset of the regular phase manifold whose configuration projection lies in a compact regular chart. For each $(q,p)\\in C$, the two scaled RATTLE equations in [[def-regular-classical-rattle-step-map]] have unique local roots in neighborhoods of\n$$\\lambda_0=\\mu_0=\\frac12A(q)^{-1}\\bigl(D^2c(q)[v,v]-J(q)M^{-1}\\nabla V(q)\\bigr),\\qquad v=M^{-1}p.$$\nIn local phase coordinates the position root depends smoothly on $(h,q,p)$, and the momentum root depends smoothly on $(h,q,p,\\lambda)$ when the position multiplier is treated as a parameter near its selected root. The local branches agree on overlaps after shrinking their neighborhoods. A finite cover of $C$ therefore gives a common $h_0(C)>0$ for $|h|<h_0(C)$; the derivatives of each fixed finite order are uniformly bounded on this cover, and the two multiplier Jacobians remain uniformly invertible there. The exact position roots can also be kept in an ambient neighborhood of the compact regular configuration projection where $J$ has full row rank, so their constrained positions remain in $Q_{\\mathrm{reg}}$. At $h=0$ both Jacobians equal $-A(q)$.",
